        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: let plugin tools yield turns",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nPlugin tools can send work to an external interaction surface, but before this change they could only return a normal tool result. The agent loop could then continue in the same turn before the external callback arrived, which races native approval and form-card flows against the eventual user response.\n\n## Why This Is Better Than The Current Behavior\n\nThis adds a narrow runtime control request on `AgentToolResult` and exposes `yieldToolResult(...)` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/tool-results`. After a plugin tool returns that result, OpenClaw retains the successful tool result and routes through the existing `sessions_yield` turn-handoff path. A later inbound event can then resume the same session.\n\nControl is applied only after the complete `afterToolCall` finalization lifecycle. Hook-added and hook-replaced controls therefore affect the actual runtime action, and runtimes without a control handler fail explicitly instead of silently continuing.\n\nThe implementation remains channel-agnostic. Existing tools and plugins are unchanged when they return no `control` field.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPlugin authors can implement native interaction tools, such as approval or form-card prompts, without racing the model loop against the user callback. Existing plugin tools do not need configuration or migration.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add `AgentToolResult.control` and the public `yieldToolResult(...)` helper.\n- Add a host-owned finalized-result control seam in agent-core.\n- Wire embedded OpenClaw sessions to the existing `sessions_yield` lifecycle.\n- Preserve result control through normal, deferred-directory, Tool Search, and Code Mode catalog execution paths.\n- Reject unsupported finalized controls with an explicit tool error.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real external plugin runtime proof\n\nEnvironment: macOS arm64, Node 22.23.1, rebased on current main.\n\nA standalone external plugin was loaded from its real manifest through `loadOpenClawPlugins`, registered and resolved `proof_ask_user`, imported `yieldToolResult` from the public Plugin SDK entrypoint, and executed through a real `Agent`. The first run yielded; the finalized successful tool result remained in the transcript; a later inbound prompt on the same Agent completed normally.\n\nRedacted observed output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plugin\": {\n    \"id\": \"yield-proof\",\n    \"loaded\": true,\n    \"registeredTools\": [\"proof_ask_user\"],\n    \"resolvedTool\": \"proof_ask_user\"\n  },\n  \"finalizedResult\": {\n    \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Question card sent.\" }],\n    \"details\": {\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"question\": \"Approve the deployment?\",\n      \"cardId\": \"proof-card-1\"\n    },\n    \"control\": {\n      \"type\": \"yield\",\n      \"message\": \"Waiting for proof card answer\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"runtime\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"proof-session-1\",\n    \"yieldEvents\": [\"Waiting for proof card answer\"],\n    \"yieldDetected\": true,\n    \"modelCalls\": 2,\n    \"retainedToolResult\": {\n      \"toolName\": \"proof_ask_user\",\n      \"details\": { \"status\": \"pending\", \"cardId\": \"proof-card-1\" },\n      \"isError\": false\n    },\n    \"resumedAssistant\": {\n      \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Answer accepted.\" }],\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Finalization and resume coverage\n\n- Agent-core tests prove controls added or replaced by `afterToolCall` are the values applied by the runtime.\n- Agent-core tests prove an unsupported finalized control becomes an explicit tool error.\n- Catalog-path coverage proves Tool Search / Code Mode preserves plugin result control.\n- Embedded orchestration coverage proves a yielded run reports `paused` / `end_turn`, releases the active session, and accepts a later inbound turn on the same session.\n\n### Verification\n\n- 68 focused tests passed across agent-core, embedded-agent, adapter, catalog, session-yield, and Plugin SDK suites.\n- Package tests type-check: `test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.packages.json`.\n- Agent tests type-check: `test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.agents.json`.\n- Plugin SDK declaration build passes: `tsconfig.plugin-sdk.dts.json`.\n- Plugin SDK API baseline, surface budgets, and export synchronization checks pass.\n- Changed TypeScript/JavaScript files pass Oxfmt and Oxlint; `git diff --check` passes.\n\n## Notes\n\nPrepared with AI assistance.\n\n## Linked Issue\n\nCloses #109761\n",
